# Block `xmlns` attribute order

On every document root (`<block>` or a type tag), declare attributes in this order — nothing interleaved.

## 1. Default XML namespace

```xml
xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
```

`xmlns:xsi` and `xsi:schemaLocation` are omitted by default (doc:DocumentFormat). XSD is not the authoring validator.

## 2. Package xmlns bindings

After the default xmlns, declare every `xmlns:<prefix>="<package.fqn>"` binding:

1. **BlockML packages** (`org.blockml.*`) first
2. **Domain packages** next — one group per domain root (e.g. all `com.machineblocks.*`, then any other domain)

Within each group, sort by package FQN (hierarchical / alphabetical).

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD — package groups interleaved -->
<playground:MyLatestStory
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:mbtype="com.machineblocks.bml.type"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:playground="org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground">

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<playground:MyLatestStory
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:playground="org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground"
  xmlns:mbtype="com.machineblocks.bml.type">

  <name>MyLatestStory</name>
```

Legacy `<block>` plus `<type>` uses the same attribute order. Keep `xsi:schemaLocation` only on files that already have it; do not add it to new documents.
